All should be fun.  But not all should be equal; simply because the task
of trying to make them all equal is doomed to failure.  There will
always be an "easiest", and always a "hardest".

Figure rather that all roles' difficulty should fall into a set range;
for example, if difficulty were possible to measure on a universal
scale, and that scale ranged from 1 meaning "a baby can do this first
try" to 10 meaning "Hawking thinks this is hard", perhaps the range
should be anywhere between 4 and 6.

Or whatever abstract range you want to set for yourself.  What it comes
down to is that it's OK for something to be the best, because something
always will be.  The roles should be comparable, but not identical.

